      "topic": "Weighted Mean & Average Profit",
      "questionText": "A firm of readymade garments makes both men's and women's shirts. Its profit average is 6% of sales. Its profit in men's shirts average 8% of sales, and women's shirts comprise 60% of output. What is the average profit per sales rupee in women's shirts?",
      "tables": [],
      "answer": {
        "status": "complete",
        "steps": [
          "Let total sales output = 100.",
          "Women's shirts comprise 60% of output ($w_1 = 60$), and Men's shirts comprise 40% of output ($w_2 = 40$).",
          "Overall profit = $6\\% \\times 100 = 6$.",
          "Profit from Men's shirts = $8\\% \\times 40 = 3.2$.",
          "Profit from Women's shirts = $6 - 3.2 = 2.8$.",
          "Average profit per sales rupee in Women's shirts = $\\frac{2.8}{60} = 0.0467$ or $4.67\\%$."
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "4.67% per sales rupee (or 0.0467)",
        "tableValuesUsed": "None",
        "sourceLink": "https://chatgpt.com/share/6af4959d-3f40-83ee-a7bc-7562286c5b1b"
      },
