      "questionText": "Calculate the quartile deviation of the following observations: 15, 20, 28, 35, 22, 27, 44, 48, 55, 50 and 60.",
      "tables": [],
      "answer": {
        "status": "complete",
        "steps": [
          "Arrange data in ascending order ($n=11$): 15, 20, 22, 27, 28, 35, 44, 48, 50, 55, 60.",
          "$Q_1 = \\text{value of } \\frac{n+1}{4} = \\frac{12}{4} = 3\\text{rd observation} = 22$.",
          "$Q_3 = \\text{value of } \\frac{3(n+1)}{4} = \\frac{36}{4} = 9\\text{th observation} = 50$.",
          "Quartile Deviation $QD = \\frac{Q_3 - Q_1}{2} = \\frac{50 - 22}{2} = \\frac{28}{2} = 14$."
        ],
        "finalAnswer": "Quartile Deviation QD = 14",
        "tableValuesUsed": "None",
